=== 01:27 UTC 2026-09-13 PRE-REGISTRATION -- ARM G: basin sampling on 06 (35B), survey OFF vs ON, written before launch
Why: ADR-0164 refused the workspace survey default-on on the strength of ONE pinned basin (E2: 06 0/3 byte-identical
on the fixed build) against ONE other (ADR-0162: 3/3), and E3 showed the no-survey basin itself moved between
22:5x (13 turns, emitter 0c2bf7b9) and 00:24 (9 turns, 091a99d3; one 56-turn run). Three identical runs of a
deterministic pod are one sample of one basin (ADR-0160: repeats are not samples), so N=3 pinned cells cannot
measure a near-tie task's pass RATE, with or without the survey. Under --no-pin, run_task.py gives every run a
fresh mkdtemp workspace path, which changes the absolute paths in the system prompt and every tool result -- a
semantically neutral perturbation. Six such runs per arm sample six basins.
Cells: 06-plugin-conventions on zds-qwen3.6-35b, --no-pin, ZAKCODE_TEMPERATURE=0, ZAKCODE_STABLE_PROMPT_IDENTITY=1,
buffered driver, build main@58281bd (prompt.py sha256 bb341dba8feb), zc-01, dumps on. Arms: NOSURVEY (default)
and SURVEY (ZAKCODE_CONTEXT_WORKSPACE_SURVEY=1), interleaved in threes: NOSURVEY x3, SURVEY x3, NOSURVEY x3,
SURVEY x3 (12 runs), so pod drift falls on both arms alike.
Rules:
  G1 instrument: every run reports a distinct workspace path (the perturbation happened); each arm's 6 runs are
     judged on verify_rc only. If an arm's 6 outputs are byte-identical despite 6 paths, the path is not a
     perturbation for that prompt -- record, and the arm's rate is one basin again (no verdict from it).
  G2 outcome: p0 = NOSURVEY passes /6, p1 = SURVEY passes /6.
     p1 <= p0 - 3  -> the survey moves 06 toward failing basins; ADR-0164's refusal stands on a sampled basis.
     |p1 - p0| <= 1 -> 06 is a coin either way and the survey is not the cause; E1 holds in the sampled sense,
                       E2/E3/E5 held in arm E, E4 is a pinned-mode property the survey does not touch (its block
                       is deterministic) -> ship the survey default-on (ADR-0164 addendum), stating the coin.
     p0 - p1 == 2  -> ambiguous at N=6; record; no ship; a later night doubles N.
  G3 turns: median turns per arm recorded (arm E: 13 -> 9 on 06); explanatory, not a verdict.
  G4 the 56-turn / 25-turn hole: count runs per arm that exceed 20 turns; explanatory.
Prediction: p0 = 4-5 of 6 (06 is near-tie on this model tonight); no prediction for p1 -- that is the question.
